        "runId": "ada-en-mw63klk3-vv0roc62-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6.1",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "Word p0028–p0029 covers the ascent and statue but lacks the hotel return, and its panorama includes an unsupported stadium superlative absent from the current day block."
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we head to Corcovado to see Christ the Redeemer. A small train takes you from the station through dense forest to the summit, where the 38-metre statue towers over Rio.\n\nChrist the Redeemer has stood here since 1931 and is one of the city’s best-known landmarks. From the summit you can see Rio, the ocean, beaches, mountains and built-up neighbourhoods. It’s a viewpoint that shows how the city fits into its natural surroundings.\n\nAfter the tour, return to the hotel and relax."
    },
